tes in two segments: CarMax Sales Operations and CarMax Auto Finance. The CarMax Sales Operations segment offers customers a range of makes and models of used vehicles, including domestic, imported, and luxury vehicles, as well as hybrid and electric vehicles; wholesale auctions; extended protection plans to customers at the time of sale; and reconditioning and vehicle repair services. The CarMax Auto Finance segment provides financing alternatives for retail customers across a range of credit spectrum and arrangements with various financial institutions. The company was founded in 1993 and is based in Richmond, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Keith  Barr | CEO, President & Director | Age 54","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 28K people. Revenue per employee of $924K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 7%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $44K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["CarMax Inc is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $7.3B market cap on $25.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 13% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $1.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 7.21\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 23.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 3.5\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 8.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 103% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.0273849202774525},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 50/100): roic below cost of capital; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 32% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Large open-market insider purchases (net $1.3M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Shift Into GEAR Plan Might Change The Case For Investing In CarMax (KMX)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/retail/nyse-kmx/carmax/news/shift-into-gear-plan-might-change-the-case-for-investing-in","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794003511.746,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.929,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"KMX or GPC: Which Is the Better Value Stock Right Now?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/kmx-gpc-better-value-stock-154002956.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793979602.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.874,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CarMax (KMX) Climbed, But What Is Driving Attention Now?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/carmax-kmx-climbed-driving-attention-162112093.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793895672.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.961,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CarMax (KMX) Stock Looks Stretched Against Its Current Earnings Power","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/retail/nyse-kmx/carmax/news/carmax-kmx-stock-looks-stretched-against-its-current-earning","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793881577.516,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.19,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"How Growth Plan At CarMax (KMX) Has Changed Its Investment Story","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/growth-plan-carmax-kmx-changed-121254920.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793880774.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.893,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags"